<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Spicer details new share issues.</title>
<headline>Spicer details new share issues.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spicer-Mitchell Holdings Ltd said on Monday it had issued 3,4-million new ordinary shares of one cent each at 70 cents a share.</p>
<p>The group said subsidiary City Investment Holdings Ltd had issued 7,1-million new ordinary shares of one cent each at 90 cents a share, raising 2.4 million rand and 6.4 million rand respectively.</p>
<p>They would be listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange on Monday, the group said, warning that negotiations could affect share prices.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
